meta {
  name: Update Order
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "QUOTE",
    "quotationStatus": "DRAFT",
    "quotationValidTill": "2026-07-25",
    "isBillGenerated": true,
    "orderNotes": "Rescheduled collection",
    "items": [
      { "id": "{{existingOrderItemId}}", "branchLabTestId": "{{branchLabTestId}}" },
      { "branchLabPanelId": "{{branchLabPanelId}}" }
    ],
    "opd": {
      "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}",
      "doctorId": "{{consultantDoctorId}}",
      "consultantType": "FOLLOW_UP",
      "visitType": "TELECONSULTATION"
    },
    "payments": [
      {
        "id": "{{existingPaymentId}}",
        "totalAmount": 3000,
        "orderDiscount": 200,
        "netAmount": 3000,
        "payableAmount": 3000,
        "paidAmount": 1500,
        "remainingBalance": 1500,
        "paymentMode": "UPI",
        "reference": "UPI-TXN-990011",
        "paymentDate": "2026-07-18"
      }
    ]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  orderId: 70f7fd0c-e902-4832-aa2c-841398df5d2d
  existingOrderItemId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  existingPaymentId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Update an order (scoped to the caller's tenant). Scalar fields (incl. `status`)
  are patched. When `items` is supplied the list is **diff-applied by stable
  `OrderItem.id`** — see the "items[] diff semantics" section below. When a
  section object (`diagnostics`/`opd`/`radiology`) is supplied it is upserted
  (created if absent, else replaced).

  ## items[] diff semantics (id-based keep / add / remove)

  Each element of `items[]` MAY carry an `id` field (the existing `OrderItem`'s
  UUID, returned by `GET /orders/:id` in `items[].id`):

  - **Include `id`** — the matching existing item row is **kept** (not removed and
    recreated, so its accession samples / reports stay linked). The row is
    identified by `id`; its mutable fields are refreshed from the payload
    (`discount`, `discountMode`, `discountValue`, `outsourceCenterId`, and — for a
    `direct` line — `unitPrice`; catalogue prices are re-resolved server-side).
    Re-send the `branchLabTestId`/`branchLabPanelId` for clarity.
  - **Omit `id`** — the element is treated as a **new** item to add; the server
    creates a fresh `OrderItem` row from its fields (`branchLabTestId`,
    `branchLabPanelId`, or `direct` + optional `outsourceCenterId`, `discount`,
    `unitPrice` — same rules as Create Order).
  - **Existing item whose `id` is absent from the payload** — the server
    **removes** it (soft-deletes the row). Only items whose `id` explicitly appears
    in the request are kept; all others are dropped.

  **Removing a test whose report has already been filled or generated is blocked:**
  if any item being removed has an associated `LabReport` that has been filled or
  generated (report is not in its initial empty state), the request is rejected with
  422 `TEST_NOT_DELETABLE_AFTER_REPORT`. The entire update rolls back — no items are
  added, removed, or reordered, and the order is left unchanged.

  **Refundable-surplus on removal:** removing paid tests can cause the recomputed
  order net (`netAmount`) to drop below the amount already paid. This is intentional
  and **allowed** — the surplus becomes a refundable negative balance (the order's
  effective balance goes negative). This no longer triggers `PAYMENT_OVERPAYMENT`.
  Use `POST /orders/:id/refund` to process the refund separately.

  Each item accepts the same fields as Create Order (`branchLabTestId`,
  `branchLabPanelId`, `direct`, `outsourceCenterId`, `discount`, `discountMode`,
  `discountValue`, `unitPrice`) — see that request's docs for validation rules.

  ## Sections

  The `opd` section carries optional `departmentId` and `categoryId` (both →
  422 `ORDER_DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND` / `ORDER_CATEGORY_NOT_FOUND` on a bad ref);
  the `radiology` section carries optional `radiologistDepartmentId` and
  `radiologistCategoryId`.
  `quotationStatus` (`DRAFT`/`CONVERTED`/`EXPIRED`) and `quotationValidTill`
  (ISO date) are patchable for quotes; omit them to leave existing values intact.

  ## payments[] — immutable history, reconcile-in-place

  Payment transactions are **immutable historical records**: an update NEVER
  deletes + recreates them (doing so used to churn transaction ids, reset
  `paymentDate`, and re-stamp `collectedBy` as the editor, silently changing
  historical collection reports). When `payments` is supplied the server
  reconciles in place:

  - Each row MAY carry an `id` (an existing `PaymentDetails.id` from
    `GET /orders/:id` → `payments[].id`). A row **with a matching id is kept** —
    its `paidAmount` / `paymentMode` / `reference` / `paymentDate` / `collectedBy`
    / `createdAt` are preserved exactly; only the order-level financial snapshot
    (gross / discount / net, carried on the first/canonical row) is refreshed.
  - A row **with no id** (or an unknown id) is a genuinely new collection and is
    **appended**. Only the net-new money (summed incoming `paidAmount` −
    already-stored paid) is added, so a re-sent unchanged ledger never fabricates
    a duplicate receipt.
  - An existing payment that is simply **absent** from the payload is **left
    intact** — it is NOT removed (money is only ever returned by a REFUND row via
    `POST /orders/:id/refund` or `PATCH /orders/:id/cancel`). The edit form
    therefore locks already-collected rows; to collect more, send a new (id-less)
    row.

  Omit `payments` entirely to leave the ledger and status untouched. The order's
  `paymentStatus` / `billStatus` / `refundStatus` are recomputed from the effective
  ledger after the reconcile. Overpayment is still rejected — a supplied `payments[]`
  whose summed `paidAmount` exceeds the (post-edit) summed `netAmount` is refused
  with 422 `PAYMENT_OVERPAYMENT` and the patch rolls back. Items removed so the net
  drops below the already-paid amount (without a new `payments[]`) is allowed — the
  surplus becomes a refundable negative balance (use `POST /orders/:id/refund`).
  `patientId` is not editable.

  ## Invoice lock & cancelled-order guard

  The order is immutable (any update rejected) in two terminal states:
  - 409 `ORDER_ALREADY_INVOICED` — an active `InvoiceSourceOrder` link exists.
    Cancelling that invoice (`POST /invoices/:id/cancel`) unlocks the order.
  - 409 `ORDER_ALREADY_CANCELLED` — the order's status is `CANCELLED`. Updating a
    cancelled order would revive it while its cancellation charge, refunds and
    released phlebotomist slot stay as they were, leaving the balance/status
    inconsistent — so it is refused outright (see the dedicated 409 request).

  The order list/detail responses expose `hasInvoice` (boolean), `invoiceCode` and
  `status` so the frontend can disable the edit/cancel actions before the call.

  ## Billing Menu creator-scoped guards (by other user)

  Enforced from the branch Registration Settings against `Order.createdBy` vs the
  JWT `person_id` (legacy orders with no `createdBy` stay permissive):
  - `BillingMenu_AllowOtherUserToEditQuotation` off ⇒ editing a QUOTE (stored or
    target status) by a non-creator is refused with 403
    `QUOTATION_EDIT_BY_OTHER_USER_NOT_ALLOWED`.
  - `BillingMenu_AllowCollectionOfAmountByOtherUser` off ⇒ a non-creator supplying
    `payments` whose summed `paidAmount` differs from the stored ledger's is
    refused with 403 `PAYMENT_COLLECTION_BY_OTHER_USER_NOT_ALLOWED`. An unchanged
    ledger (or omitting `payments`) is allowed, so non-payment edits still work.

  ## Finalization validation (draft → live)
  
  Whenever this patch lands the order in a LIVE status (`ORDER` / `QUOTE` /
  `APPOINTMENT`) — e.g. finalizing a draft with `{ "status": "ORDER" }` — the
  server enforces the same required-field checks as Create Order, evaluated on the
  EFFECTIVE order (this patch merged over the persisted draft). So a bare status
  flip still validates the draft's stored items/diagnostics. Rejections (the whole
  update rolls back, the draft is left unchanged):
  - 422 `ORDER_REQUIRES_ITEMS` — the order has no items (neither in this patch nor
    already persisted).
  - 422 `ORDER_HOME_VISIT_PHLEBOTOMIST_REQUIRED` — home-visit diagnostics with no
    phlebotomist.
  - 422 `ORDER_HOME_VISIT_SLOT_REQUIRED` — home-visit diagnostics with no
    collection date/time.
  - 422 `APPOINTMENT_SECTION_REQUIRED` — status `APPOINTMENT` with no scheduled
    section.
  Saving as `DRAFT` skips all of these, so incomplete drafts remain saveable.
  
  ## Home-visit slot reservation on edit
  
  The phlebotomist slot reservation is re-pointed when the booking changes
  (reschedule, phlebotomist swap, home-visit toggle, or a status flip into/out of
  `APPOINTMENT`): the old opening is released and the new one reserved atomically
  in the same transaction. If nothing about the booking changed, the reservation
  is left untouched (an unchanged past appointment is not re-validated). Re-pointing
  can be rejected with the same codes as create — 404
  `PHLEBOTOMIST_SCHEDULE_FOR_STAFF_NOT_FOUND`, 422 `PHLEBOTOMIST_SLOT_UNAVAILABLE`,
  409 `PHLEBOTOMIST_SLOT_FULL`, 409 `PHLEBOTOMIST_DAILY_CAP_REACHED` — in which
  case the whole update rolls back and the original reservation is preserved.
}
